WEBVTT

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:04.550
What a tragedy this turned out to be.

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:09.450
There's no way we can build mutual 
trust with the people now.

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:12.700
<i>Even if I knew it would bring us victory,</i>

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:15.720
<i>I could never bring myself 
to be this thorough.</i>

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:20.460
<i>Well done indeed, Count Lohengramm.</i>

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:25.150
Our navy will take back 
the captured territory,

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:27.450
while delivering food to the people.

00:00:27.450 --> 00:00:31.370
Do not let those arrogant 
insurgents return home alive.

00:00:32.010 --> 00:00:33.880
I expect the best from all of you.

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:35.680
Prosit!

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:37.520
Prosit!

00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:39.470
Prosit!

00:02:12.690 --> 00:02:20.950
<b>Legend of the Galactic Heroes</b>

00:02:31.970 --> 00:02:33.710
Enemy cargo ship convoy located.

00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:37.970
They're moving along the standard Imperial 
route within possible warp range.

00:02:41.870 --> 00:02:43.040
Checkmate.

00:02:44.660 --> 00:02:47.100
<i>Sir, please report to the 
bridge immediately.</i>

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:58.860
What is it? Did something 
happen at the front line?

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:01.980
The front line? <i>This</i> is the front line!

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:03.860
Can you not see that?!

00:03:04.510 --> 00:03:07.810
Ships approaching detection range! 
It appears to be the Imperial fleet!

00:03:07.810 --> 00:03:11.020
There are 8,000... 
no, 10,000... no, 15,000...

00:03:11.380 --> 00:03:12.970
Over 20,000 ships!

00:03:13.550 --> 00:03:14.630
Impossible!

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:20.860
They sent such a huge force 
against a mere supply convoy?

00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:23.010
Why?!

00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:24.890
<u></u>Vice Admiral Siegfried Kircheis

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:28.580
Message from Admiral Kircheis.

00:03:28.950 --> 00:03:30.930
The enemy's supply convoy is destroyed.

00:03:31.450 --> 00:03:35.070
Of our fleet, only one ship suffered damage.

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:41.100
We've now succeeded in cutting 
off the enemy's supply line.

00:03:42.450 --> 00:03:43.930
Connect me to all admirals.

00:03:49.840 --> 00:03:51.960
In accordance with the established plan,

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:54.400
strike the rebels with full force.

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:55.340
<i>Yes, sir.</i>

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:04.340
<b>Episode 12</b>

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:04.340
<b>The Verge of Death (Part 2)</b>

00:04:10.430 --> 00:04:13.350
<u></u>Alliance Navy 10th Fleet

00:04:12.930 --> 00:04:16.440
Unable to establish communication with 
the patrol ship since it notified us

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:18.190
that the enemy fleet was located.

00:04:18.580 --> 00:04:19.590
They're coming.

00:04:20.080 --> 00:04:23.740
Send a message to headquarters 
and all fleet commanders.

00:04:23.740 --> 00:04:26.220
Tell them we've encountered the enemy.

00:04:26.220 --> 00:04:27.070
Yes, sir.

00:04:27.510 --> 00:04:31.660
<i>If only we'd made up our 
minds to withdraw sooner...</i>

00:04:27.910 --> 00:04:32.370
<u>10th Fleet Commander
</u>Vice Admiral Ulanhu

00:04:32.370 --> 00:04:35.590
Message to all ships!
Prepare for fleet action!

00:04:47.140 --> 00:04:49.100
<u>Imperial Navy Black Lancers Flagship
</u>Königstiger

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:51.560
<u></u>Vice Admiral Fritz Joseph Bittenfeld

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:56.020
The enemy has started firing, most likely 
from a blind spot behind the planet.

00:04:56.020 --> 00:04:58.680
No geographical advantage 
can triumph over unity.

00:05:00.250 --> 00:05:03.490
The 13th Fleet will come 
to rescue us soon enough!

00:05:03.490 --> 00:05:07.150
This is Miracle Yang we're 
talking about! Victory is assured!

00:05:08.580 --> 00:05:09.900
<i>At the same time,</i>

00:05:09.910 --> 00:05:11.870
<u>7th Fleet Commander
</u>Vice Admiral Hawood

00:05:10.550 --> 00:05:12.700
<i>the Imperial Navy was attacking</i>

00:05:11.870 --> 00:05:13.580
<u>3rd Fleet Commander
</u>Vice Admiral Lefebvre

00:05:12.700 --> 00:05:15.340
<i>each of the Alliance fleets in turn.</i>

00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:15.330
<u>8th Fleet Commander
</u>Vice Admiral Appleton

00:05:15.330 --> 00:05:17.040
<u>12th Fleet Commander
</u>Vice Admiral Borodin

00:05:17.630 --> 00:05:19.460
Go full defensive and retreat!

00:05:17.670 --> 00:05:20.250
<u>9th Fleet Commander
</u>Vice Admiral al-Salem

00:05:19.460 --> 00:05:20.250
Yes, sir!

00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:25.510
<u>5th Fleet Commander
</u>Vice Admiral Alexandre Bewcock

00:05:21.330 --> 00:05:23.460
Did we miss our chance to retreat?

00:05:24.050 --> 00:05:27.250
Our line is stretched out so far, 
we can't keep it supplied.

00:05:27.250 --> 00:05:30.220
How long can we hold out like this?

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:33.180
<u></u>Alliance Navy 13th Fleet

00:05:31.270 --> 00:05:33.180
Message from Admiral Ulanhu.

00:05:33.440 --> 00:05:38.460
"My fleet will engage with the enemy 
at 16:07 standard Alliance time."

00:05:38.820 --> 00:05:40.180
So it's time...

00:05:40.180 --> 00:05:43.560
Withdrawal from the occupied 
territory is complete.

00:05:43.560 --> 00:05:45.510
Shall we start moving?

00:05:45.510 --> 00:05:47.160
No, we'll stay here.

00:05:48.260 --> 00:05:52.970
Due to heavy gases in this starzone, 
the range for optical weapons is short.

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:57.160
We'll confuse the enemy with close combat 
and watch for our chance to break out.

00:05:59.260 --> 00:06:01.770
Have the  get ready.

00:06:01.770 --> 00:06:02.520
Yes, sir...

00:06:03.140 --> 00:06:07.050
This is our first battle since 
joining the 13th Fleet.

00:06:03.460 --> 00:06:07.050
<u></u>Lieutenant Olivier Poplin

00:06:07.050 --> 00:06:10.260
<u></u>Lieutenant Warren Hughes

00:06:07.050 --> 00:06:10.260
I was wondering what we'd do if 
we ended up just going home.

00:06:10.260 --> 00:06:13.710
I was getting out of shape. 
This'll be the perfect workout.

00:06:10.260 --> 00:06:13.720
Lieutenant Saleh Aziz Shakely

00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:16.680
<u></u>Lieutenant Ivan Konev

00:06:16.680 --> 00:06:21.990
Let's show 'em what us guys from the 88th 
Independent Air Combat Unit can do.

00:06:32.480 --> 00:06:34.760
Let's get this over with fast.

00:06:34.760 --> 00:06:36.640
Keep the champagne cold for us.

00:06:36.640 --> 00:06:38.520
<i>You know we don't have any.</i>

00:06:38.520 --> 00:06:40.820
<i>I'll, at least, have some 
water ready for you.</i>

00:06:42.640 --> 00:06:43.990
Not romantic at all, man.

00:06:50.650 --> 00:06:51.960
<i>Permission granted to launch.</i>

00:06:51.960 --> 00:06:53.800
Roger. Launching.

00:07:19.180 --> 00:07:20.330
Down you go!

00:07:26.840 --> 00:07:29.080
Damn, what the hell?!

00:07:33.760 --> 00:07:35.720
The output isn't increasing!

00:07:36.150 --> 00:07:37.260
Crap!

00:07:45.700 --> 00:07:46.770
Hughes!

00:07:47.630 --> 00:07:49.620
Margin of error is seven... 
no, eight degrees?

00:08:09.910 --> 00:08:11.610
Th-The airframe is...

00:08:12.510 --> 00:08:15.130
Shakely, don't push it! Return to base!

00:08:15.130 --> 00:08:16.570
<i>They've locked on to me!</i>

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:34.270
My firing line was off by 
nine to twelve degrees!

00:08:34.640 --> 00:08:38.040
If my machine gun is useless in a 
battle where lasers don't work,

00:08:38.040 --> 00:08:40.090
I might as well be unarmed!

00:08:40.580 --> 00:08:41.820
I'm sorry.

00:08:41.330 --> 00:08:46.880
Engineer Lieutenant Toda

00:08:41.820 --> 00:08:44.240
Forgive me if the maintenance was faulty,

00:08:44.620 --> 00:08:46.660
but since our supplies were cut off,

00:08:46.660 --> 00:08:49.710
all of us mechanics have had 
nothing to eat or drink,

00:08:50.150 --> 00:08:52.550
unlike you pilots.

00:08:58.450 --> 00:09:01.290
Sorry. I honestly apologize for being rude.

00:09:01.710 --> 00:09:04.020
I'd like you to adjust my 
machine gun right away.

00:09:04.380 --> 00:09:05.640
Will you do it?

00:09:06.110 --> 00:09:08.570
Hughes and Shakely were killed.

00:09:08.570 --> 00:09:10.530
This'll be a vicious battle.

00:09:10.900 --> 00:09:12.550
We're counting on all of you.

00:09:12.990 --> 00:09:15.820
We're going back out there once 
the maintenance is done!

00:09:15.820 --> 00:09:16.740
Yes, sir!

00:09:17.520 --> 00:09:19.470
I won't mess it up this time.

00:09:20.800 --> 00:09:23.580
So please, Lieutenant, win this for us.

00:09:23.980 --> 00:09:25.130
You got it.

00:09:25.130 --> 00:09:29.220
We'll show those Imperial bastards 
that the 13th Fleet Air Combat Unit

00:09:29.220 --> 00:09:32.040
is a force to be reckoned with.

00:09:33.420 --> 00:09:36.220
<u>Imperial Navy Lutz Fleet Flagship
</u>Herðubreið

00:09:42.880 --> 00:09:45.590
The enemy has fired a 
high-output energy blast!

00:09:43.220 --> 00:09:47.440
<u></u>Alliance Navy 12th Fleet

00:09:45.590 --> 00:09:47.150
It's headed toward us!

00:09:48.740 --> 00:09:50.350
Destruction of enemy ship confirmed.

00:09:50.350 --> 00:09:51.900
Long-range attack successful.

00:09:52.470 --> 00:09:55.810
Already, 80% of the enemy's 
ships are immobilized.

00:09:55.820 --> 00:09:58.780
<u></u>Vice Admiral Cornelius Lutz

00:10:14.460 --> 00:10:16.800
<u>Imperial Navy Reuenthal Fleet Flagship
</u>Tristan

00:10:17.130 --> 00:10:19.760
<u></u>Alliance Navy 5th Fleet

00:10:19.770 --> 00:10:23.920
Deploy all ships to the front 
and go full defensive!

00:10:23.920 --> 00:10:27.110
Deploy all cruisers taking refuge 
at the rear to both flanks,

00:10:27.110 --> 00:10:29.420
and strike the enemy from both directions!

00:10:29.420 --> 00:10:31.610
Hold formation and don't panic.

00:10:31.610 --> 00:10:33.320
Keep our escape route open!

00:10:34.360 --> 00:10:39.460
<i>This opponent doesn't look like one who'll 
give up victory easily, though...</i>

00:10:43.720 --> 00:10:44.680
Well...

00:10:45.200 --> 00:10:47.620
The enemy certainly is cunning.

00:10:45.330 --> 00:10:47.960
<u></u>Vice Admiral Oskar von Reuenthal

00:10:48.580 --> 00:10:51.830
<u></u>Alliance Navy 9th Fleet

00:10:56.890 --> 00:10:59.340
Enemy fleet approaching from starboard!

00:10:59.690 --> 00:11:01.790
They're within physical firing range!

00:11:01.790 --> 00:11:02.720
What?

00:11:02.720 --> 00:11:06.600
Their data link shouldn't be 
functioning. It's too soon!

00:11:08.490 --> 00:11:11.150
It couldn't be... Gale Wolf?

00:11:12.310 --> 00:11:15.900
<u>Imperial Navy Mittermeyer Fleet Flagship
</u>Beowulf

00:11:16.380 --> 00:11:18.790
Don't rush and get too close.

00:11:16.730 --> 00:11:21.110
<u></u>Vice Admiral Wolfgang Mittermeyer

00:11:18.790 --> 00:11:21.010
They might counter when we least expect it.

00:11:21.590 --> 00:11:27.660
Of course, that's assuming the rebels 
can manage a fleet worth a damn...

00:11:27.660 --> 00:11:30.120
<u></u>Alliance Navy 13th Fleet

00:11:32.370 --> 00:11:34.920
<u>Imperial Navy Wahlen Fleet Flagship
</u>Salamander

00:11:34.920 --> 00:11:37.000
Vice Admiral August Samuel Wahlen

00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:39.470
<u></u>Alliance Navy 8th Fleet

00:11:41.680 --> 00:11:44.140
<u>Imperial Navy Mecklinger Fleet Flagship
</u>Gandharva

00:11:44.140 --> 00:11:46.600
Vice Admiral Ernest Mecklinger

00:11:47.220 --> 00:11:51.690
<u></u>Imperial Navy Kircheis Fleet

00:11:49.490 --> 00:11:52.150
The enemy fleet is leaving the theater.

00:11:52.590 --> 00:11:55.190
We've lost 90% of our ships.

00:11:52.600 --> 00:11:55.610
<u></u>Alliance Navy 7th Fleet

00:11:55.190 --> 00:11:58.430
Organized battle is no longer possible.

00:12:00.360 --> 00:12:04.790
We're a flagship, and we were discarded 
without being so much as a threat.

00:12:07.700 --> 00:12:10.290
We have taken control of 
this sector of space.

00:12:10.290 --> 00:12:12.410
Dominion is entirely ours.

00:12:12.410 --> 00:12:16.370
And you're telling me we still 
can't annihilate them?

00:12:16.750 --> 00:12:19.340
<u>Chief Adjutant
</u>Captain Eugen

00:12:17.410 --> 00:12:18.520
Close in.

00:12:19.330 --> 00:12:20.960
Be thorough about it.

00:12:20.960 --> 00:12:21.710
Yes, sir.

00:12:26.460 --> 00:12:30.610
We only have about a thousand ships left 
that can fight, including this one.

00:12:30.610 --> 00:12:33.480
We can't continue this battle any longer.

00:12:33.760 --> 00:12:36.510
We'll have to choose between 
surrendering and fleeing.

00:12:36.510 --> 00:12:38.900
That's a disgraceful pair of options.

00:12:38.900 --> 00:12:39.770
Isn't it?

00:12:40.330 --> 00:12:43.430
Surrender isn't my style. We'll flee.

00:12:43.950 --> 00:12:48.330
Are there any surviving fleet commanders 
among the remaining ships?

00:12:48.680 --> 00:12:51.060
Commodore Attenborough is still alive.

00:12:52.870 --> 00:12:54.620
Commodore Dusty Attenborough

00:12:55.590 --> 00:12:58.570
I'll open an escape route for us.

00:12:58.570 --> 00:13:02.870
Commodore, you lead the ships that 
can no longer fight in escaping.

00:13:03.240 --> 00:13:04.890
<i>Admiral Ulanhu...</i>

00:13:05.310 --> 00:13:07.170
I'm counting on you, Commodore.

00:13:08.560 --> 00:13:11.710
Bearing: two o'clock. 
All ships, maximum battle speed!

00:13:17.010 --> 00:13:18.770
Follow us! Stay close!

00:13:30.940 --> 00:13:32.160
What?!

00:13:37.580 --> 00:13:40.270
We can get through! 
The escape route is open!

00:13:43.650 --> 00:13:45.510
What's the status of our allies?

00:13:46.020 --> 00:13:48.980
About half of our ships survived.

00:13:49.390 --> 00:13:50.680
I see...

00:13:55.260 --> 00:13:57.640
<i>After receiving a fierce attack 
from the Imperial Navy,</i>

00:13:57.640 --> 00:14:03.130
<i>the Alliance Navy's expeditionary force was 
left at an overwhelming disadvantage.</i>

00:14:03.740 --> 00:14:04.830
<i>However...</i>

00:14:14.040 --> 00:14:18.910
<i>The one exception was Yang's 13th Fleet.</i>

00:14:19.590 --> 00:14:22.670
The enemy air combat unit's torpedo 
attack did immense damage.

00:14:22.670 --> 00:14:24.900
We won't be able to hold formation.

00:14:26.000 --> 00:14:29.290
Are you saying we should give in to 
the rebel force's insolent tactics?

00:14:29.710 --> 00:14:32.750
We should deal with the situation 
before it ends in disgrace for us.

00:14:29.840 --> 00:14:32.760
<u>Chief Adjutant
</u>Lieutenant Lubitsch

00:14:34.140 --> 00:14:37.600
Vice Admiral Karl Gustav Kempff

00:14:34.280 --> 00:14:37.600
We'll reorganize the unit 
so we can attack further.

00:14:37.900 --> 00:14:41.560
Prepare for the enemy's pursuit 
and withdraw immediately!

00:14:42.100 --> 00:14:44.010
The enemy fleet is withdrawing!

00:14:44.010 --> 00:14:46.700
Admiral, this is a perfect 
opportunity to pursue them.

00:14:47.210 --> 00:14:48.020
No.

00:14:48.520 --> 00:14:50.660
Even if we push ourselves and win here,

00:14:50.660 --> 00:14:53.270
we can't overturn the enemy's 
overall dominance.

00:14:53.740 --> 00:14:56.230
There's only one path we can take right now.

00:14:57.410 --> 00:14:59.320
All fleets, retreat.

00:15:00.640 --> 00:15:01.480
Yes, sir!

00:15:05.900 --> 00:15:10.740
<i>Yang Wen-li's 13th Fleet, having 
escaped the Kempff Fleet,</i>

00:15:10.740 --> 00:15:14.410
<i>took a course to return to Iserlohn.</i>

00:15:15.180 --> 00:15:17.570
Report from the lead patrol ship.

00:15:17.960 --> 00:15:21.740
Multiple ships with no call 
signs sighted ahead.

00:15:22.140 --> 00:15:27.310
Vice Admiral Hawood's 7th Fleet should 
be garrisoned in that sector.

00:15:27.310 --> 00:15:29.980
There are too many of them to be his.

00:15:29.980 --> 00:15:30.890
How big?

00:15:31.650 --> 00:15:34.050
About three times as 
large as our own fleet.

00:15:34.050 --> 00:15:35.520
That'd be the enemy.

00:15:35.910 --> 00:15:40.130
We have to assume the 7th Fleet 
has already been defeated.

00:15:40.410 --> 00:15:43.330
Report. Communications with the 
patrol ship have been cut off!

00:15:43.330 --> 00:15:45.350
So it was captured.

00:15:48.560 --> 00:15:51.890
Rebel fleet located. 
They number approximately 10,000.

00:15:52.260 --> 00:15:54.980
Comparing it with the report 
from Admiral Kempff,

00:15:54.980 --> 00:15:57.880
it's most likely the 13th Fleet.

00:15:57.880 --> 00:15:59.550
Yang Wen-li?

00:16:02.320 --> 00:16:07.340
He just might be the kind of 
person you spoke of earlier.

00:16:10.170 --> 00:16:12.990
We can't miss this chance. We will attack.

00:16:13.510 --> 00:16:15.320
All ships, maximum battle speed.

00:16:15.320 --> 00:16:16.820
Command to all ships.

00:16:16.820 --> 00:16:18.570
All ships, maximum battle speed.

00:16:43.820 --> 00:16:46.240
We have no choice but to meet them.

00:16:47.890 --> 00:16:50.030
We're going to put the plan in motion now.

00:16:50.990 --> 00:16:56.410
<u></u>Iserlohn Fortress Central Command

00:16:52.500 --> 00:16:54.980
Since we received word that they'd 
encountered the Imperial Navy,

00:16:54.980 --> 00:16:57.730
none of the information we've received
makes any sense.

00:16:58.130 --> 00:17:02.760
The 3rd, 7th, 10th, and 12th Fleets 
are unable to respond.

00:16:58.620 --> 00:17:03.210
<u>Alliance Navy Integrated Tactical Operations Center Vice Chief
</u>Admiral Dwight Greenhill

00:17:02.760 --> 00:17:07.690
The 5th, 8th, 9th, and 13th Fleets 
appear to be alive and well,

00:17:07.690 --> 00:17:09.930
but we're unable to get detailed reports.

00:17:12.170 --> 00:17:17.300
<u>Alliance Space Fleet Commander-in-Chief
</u>Fleet Admiral Lassalle Lobos

00:17:12.730 --> 00:17:18.540
It seems that the High Council doesn't want 
this expedition to simply end in loss, either.

00:17:18.920 --> 00:17:20.270
What?

00:17:20.600 --> 00:17:25.230
Reorganize the scattered fleets 
and meet the enemy's attack.

00:17:25.500 --> 00:17:27.950
Relay the message to the entire navy.

00:17:30.190 --> 00:17:31.640
What is it?

00:17:31.640 --> 00:17:36.890
Well... I was just wondering if we have 
enough forces left at the front line for that.

00:17:37.570 --> 00:17:42.580
Even if we reorganize, we can't overturn the 
situation if the enemy still outnumbers us.

00:17:42.580 --> 00:17:44.070
In fact, we'd lose even more.

00:17:44.660 --> 00:17:48.560
Have the entire navy rendezvous 
at the Amritsar Starzone.

00:17:48.560 --> 00:17:49.620
Your Excellency!

00:17:49.880 --> 00:17:51.630
That is an order.

00:18:05.630 --> 00:18:09.490
The enemy is pushing us back with mainstay 
equipment in superior numbers,

00:18:09.490 --> 00:18:11.340
all while supplying their 
forces from the rear

00:18:11.340 --> 00:18:14.340
and hitting with uninterrupted firepower.

00:18:18.140 --> 00:18:20.860
We'll use a good strategy without pretense.

00:18:21.850 --> 00:18:25.670
I hear Count Lohengramm has 
a brilliant subordinate.

00:18:29.010 --> 00:18:31.420
Urgent coded message from headquarters.

00:18:31.690 --> 00:18:32.630
Read it.

00:18:33.240 --> 00:18:38.040
"Gather at point A in the Amritsar Starzone 
on the fourteenth of this month.

00:18:38.590 --> 00:18:41.890
Cease combat and relocate at once."

00:18:42.580 --> 00:18:44.550
Little late for that now!

00:18:45.130 --> 00:18:47.670
If we could retreat, 
we'd have done it by now!

00:18:48.590 --> 00:18:50.890
He says that like it's so simple.

00:18:50.890 --> 00:18:52.190
What will you do?

00:18:55.230 --> 00:18:57.920
Reorganize the fleet into line ahead formation,

00:18:57.920 --> 00:19:00.770
deploy a concentration of dreadnought 
battleships at the rear,

00:19:00.770 --> 00:19:03.630
and create a diversion while we 
find a way to leave the front.

00:19:04.760 --> 00:19:08.870
Our goal is to turn the fleet around
to head to Amritsar.

00:19:09.670 --> 00:19:13.740
Assume that leaving the front is 
our only tactical objective.

00:19:14.350 --> 00:19:18.600
Of course, the enemy has probably 
guessed what we're going to do.

00:19:18.600 --> 00:19:21.850
If this doesn't work, 
nothing we try is going to.

00:19:21.850 --> 00:19:25.650
It's the best option available 
to us at the moment.

00:19:25.650 --> 00:19:26.800
I agree.

00:19:26.800 --> 00:19:29.090
Still, the enemy has thrice our numbers.

00:19:29.090 --> 00:19:31.310
We will almost certainly 
suffer damages ourselves,

00:19:31.790 --> 00:19:34.270
but I want to minimize them.

00:19:34.710 --> 00:19:36.590
I'm counting on you all.

00:20:22.480 --> 00:20:26.030
We've never experienced such losses before.

00:20:26.030 --> 00:20:28.070
But we're almost there...

00:20:41.540 --> 00:20:43.550
Search system has located multiple ships!

00:20:43.550 --> 00:20:44.560
What?!

00:20:44.560 --> 00:20:46.670
The enemy had a detached force?

00:20:47.640 --> 00:20:49.210
We've ID'd their call sign!

00:20:51.480 --> 00:20:54.010
It's Admiral Hawood's 7th Fleet!

00:20:55.680 --> 00:20:56.730
That's...

00:21:08.490 --> 00:21:11.450
We will back up the 
13th Fleet as they withdraw!

00:21:11.730 --> 00:21:14.660
Don't worry about how much energy is left!

00:21:14.660 --> 00:21:16.910
Fire all we've got at them!

00:21:33.780 --> 00:21:37.390
Don't make the wrong choice, Yang Wen-li.

00:21:37.690 --> 00:21:39.900
We can attack if we act now!

00:21:40.860 --> 00:21:42.430
We'll continue to withdraw.

00:21:42.430 --> 00:21:43.450
But...

00:21:44.090 --> 00:21:46.470
It's a tough decision, but, Admiral...

00:21:46.970 --> 00:21:48.560
You're right.

00:22:06.670 --> 00:22:10.620
Even as they flee, the enemy is 
maintaining order in its own way.

00:22:10.620 --> 00:22:14.070
It looks like they're headed 
for the Amritsar Starzone.

00:22:14.070 --> 00:22:17.060
That's close to the Iserlohn 
Corridor entrance.

00:22:17.450 --> 00:22:20.480
But I find it hard to believe 
they're merely fleeing there.

00:22:21.130 --> 00:22:22.690
What do you think?

00:22:23.700 --> 00:22:27.070
I suspect they intend to gather 
there and renew their attack.

00:22:27.710 --> 00:22:30.240
What will you do about it, Your Excellency?

00:22:30.630 --> 00:22:34.330
Obviously, our navy will gather 
at Amritsar, as well.

00:22:35.400 --> 00:22:39.150
If Amritsar is the place they 
want as their graveyard,

00:22:39.780 --> 00:22:42.660
I think we should grant their wish.

00:22:45.770 --> 00:22:48.360
<i>In the year UC 796,</i>

00:22:48.360 --> 00:22:52.720
<i>or the 487th year of the Galactic 
Imperial calendar, on October 14th,</i>

00:22:53.540 --> 00:22:57.310
<i>the Galactic Imperial Navy set a 
course for the Amritsar Starzone,</i>

00:22:57.310 --> 00:23:02.110
<i>the place chosen by the Free Planets 
Alliance for a decisive battle.</i>

00:23:03.740 --> 00:23:05.560
<i>Yang Wen-li</i>

00:23:05.970 --> 00:23:08.750
<i>and Reinhard von Lohengramm...</i>

00:23:09.690 --> 00:23:15.960
<i>Both heroes will meet once again at Amritsar.</i>
